          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Scope Map",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Thing",
                "Scope"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Region",
                  "isolated area, ==3+ AZs=="
                ],
                [
                  "AZ",
                  "one or more data centres"
                ],
                [
                  "VPC",
                  "one Region, spans **all** its AZs"
                ],
                [
                  "Subnet",
                  "exactly ==one AZ=="
                ],
                [
                  "IAM",
                  "{purple:global}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Primary CIDR between ==/16 and /28==, e.g. `10.0.0.0/16`",
                "Keep it clear of other VPCs and on-prem ranges"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Surviving an AZ Failure",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "VPC",
                    "sub": "10.0.0.0/16",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Subnet",
                    "sub": "AZ-a",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Subnet",
                    "sub": "AZ-b",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==One subnet per AZ==, in at least **2 AZs**",
                "Spread instances across them"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Overlapping CIDRs block ==VPC peering== and VPN",
                "Primary CIDR cannot be changed later",
                "Default VPC used for production"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Subnet regional or zonal?** Zonal: one AZ.",
                "**Survive an AZ failure?** Subnets and instances in 2+ AZs.",
                "**Why CIDR for peering?** Overlapping ranges cannot be routed."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Subnets, Route Tables, IGW and NAT",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Subnets, Route Tables, IGW and NAT",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Makes a Subnet Public",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Public== subnet: route `0.0.0.0/0` → IGW",
                "Private: no IGW route; the label comes from the **route**",
                "One route table per subnet; ==longest prefix== wins",
                "`local` VPC-CIDR route: always present, undeletable"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. IGW vs NAT",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "IGW",
                "NAT gateway"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Cost",
                  "Free",
                  "Hourly + per GB"
                ],
                [
                  "Traffic",
                  "In and out",
                  "Outbound only"
                ],
                [
                  "Needs",
                  "Public or Elastic IP",
                  "Route `0.0.0.0/0` → nat-id"
                ],
                [
                  "Placement",
                  "VPC-wide, scales out",
                  "Zonal: public subnet + EIP"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example and HA",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Subnet",
                "Destination",
                "Target"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Public",
                  "`0.0.0.0/0`",
                  "`igw-xxx`"
                ],
                [
                  "Private",
                  "`0.0.0.0/0`",
                  "`nat-xxx`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Zonal NAT: ==one per AZ== for HA",
                "Regional NAT: one per VPC, spans AZs itself"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes and Interview Point",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Zonal NAT in a private subnet: no internet",
                "No public IP in a public subnet: no internet",
                "**What makes a subnet public?** An IGW route",
                "**NAT vs IGW?** NAT is outbound-only; IGW is two-way",
                "**Why a NAT per AZ?** A zonal NAT fails with its AZ"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Security Groups vs NACLs",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Security Groups vs NACLs",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Two Firewalls",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:SG} on the ==ENI/instance==",
                "==Stateful==: replies auto-allowed",
                "==Allow only==; default deny in, allow all out"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:NACL} on the ==subnet==",
                "==Stateless==: allow replies, ports `1024-65535`",
                "Numbered rules, ==lowest first==, first match wins",
                "Implicit deny at the end"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Compare",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "SG",
                "NACL"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Level",
                  "Instance",
                  "Subnet"
                ],
                [
                  "State",
                  "Stateful",
                  "Stateless"
                ],
                [
                  "Rules",
                  "Allow only",
                  "Allow + deny"
                ],
                [
                  "Evaluated",
                  "All rules",
                  "In order"
                ],
                [
                  "Block one IP",
                  "{red:No}",
                  "{green:Yes}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 4
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example and Mistake",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Internet",
                    "ink": "black"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Web SG",
                    "sub": "443 from 0.0.0.0/0",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "DB SG",
                    "sub": "5432 from web-SG id",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "A custom NACL without the outbound ==ephemeral range== breaks replies."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Stateful vs stateless?** SG tracks replies; NACL does not",
                "**Block one IP?** NACL deny; SG cannot",
                "**SG to SG?** Yes, use its id as source",
                "**SG open, still fails?** NACL or ephemeral ports"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
